    <h2>Attack Pattern: Brute Force</h2>
    <p>A brute force attack is an attempt to guess credentials by systematically trying many username/password combinations until one works. It is one of the most common and detectable attacks — detectable precisely because it leaves a distinctive and repetitive pattern in authentication logs.</p>

